    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Heritage of FIPA-ACL and Speech Acts Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements a pure-stdlib FIPA-ACL translator. It encodes and decodes the canonical ACL envelope and shows how every MCP / A2A message shape reduces to the same seven fields. The demo:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Encodes five MCP-style and A2A-style messages as FIPA-ACL."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Decodes FIPA-ACL back to the modern equivalent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Runs a toy Contract Net negotiation between one manager and three bidders using `cfp`, `propose`, `accept-proposal`, `reject-proposal`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output is a side-by-side trace showing each modern message in both its 2026 JSON form and its FIPA-ACL form, then a round-trip of a contract-net bid. The same protocol primitives survive the round-trip; only the syntax differs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run `code/main.py`. Observe the round-trip encoding. Identify which FIPA performative corresponds to `tools/call`, `resources/read`, and A2A task creation.\n2. Extend the contract-net demo with a `cancel` performative that lets the manager withdraw the task mid-bid. What failure case does `cancel` solve that retries alone do not?\n3. Read FIPA ACL Message Structure (http://www.fipa.org/specs/fipa00037/) sections 4.1\u20134.3. Pick one performative not covered in this lesson and describe its modern JSON-RPC analog.\n4. Read Liu et al., arXiv:2505.02279. For each of MCP, A2A, ACP, ANP, list the FIPA performative families they keep and drop.\n5. Design a minimal JSON-Schema for the `content` field of a `request` performative in your own system. What does that schema give you that pure natural-language does not, and what does it cost?"
      ]
    }
  ],
